From be650bb3402b2187e8885c2c4e520be106f9162d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:48:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): sweep XY arcs on the true circle in the field
 engine and envelope scan

The field engine (field_cut::chords) and the generator-time envelope
scan still drew G2/G3 in G17 as inscribed chords, a sagitta inside the
arc. That read false cuts at convex corners, and hid real cuts at
concave corners and on bull-nose helices, where a rim column the true
arc cuts 2.5 mm deep stood uncut on the field.

- Field engine (new field_arc.rs): an upright mill tool's XY arc is
  swept as Sweep::Arc pieces. The piece budget is unchanged, so the
  windows and the cell ceiling are too. Level pieces are exact in
  closed form (clamped bearing, the column's tie laws, closed-form
  floor entry). Helical pieces use dexel_arc's sample + golden search,
  with real evaluations only and the conservative hair.
- Envelope scan (new scan_arc.rs): each arc piece keeps arc_chords'
  chord for bins, boxes and rings. Every distance (rest, flank, hidden
  rest, facet gouge) is read off the true arc, and walks and prunes
  grow by the piece's bulge.
- stock_bull_nose is back to 1e-5 engine parity on the helix arc.

Tilted poses, lathe tools and XZ/YZ arcs keep their chords.

Fixes #413

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
